A||N||5||fropuff||0-60 Timer???||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||08-31-2000||07:03 PM||||Hey, I've been brainstorming.  I was wondering if there was a way to wire up a 0-60 timer to my Fiero to time 0-60 time and 1/4 mile time.  Does anyone know if there is one I could buy somewhere?  Thanks a bunch.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||08-31-2000||07:23 PM||||Yes, its called the G-Tech and you can get it at Summit Racing, JC Whitney, Jegs, PAW, and you name it. Just type in G-Tech on a search engine and you will find information about it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||08-31-2000||07:24 PM||||Maybe I should be a little more clear.  What I want is a "stopwatch" that I can control to start and stop when I want.  I don't want it wired up to the speedo or anything, just a stopwatch that I can control easily.  I would then wire it up to a toggle switch to activate and de-activate it.  I am looking for one that is rectangular and that will fit on the left corner of the dash by the windshield.  I would mount the toggle switch somewhere else.  Thanks a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||08-31-2000||10:55 PM||||It would be easier to just buy a G-tech.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000004||fropuff||08-31-2000||11:26 PM||||I think I'll pass on it if I have to pay $120.  I was thinking in the $40 range.  Does anyone know what I"m talking about?  I'm looking to have a rectangular "stopwatch" that is wired to a toggle switch for arm/disarm ability.  I would use the switch to start it when I take off, switch it off when I reach 60.  I also want to see a quarter mile time.  I don't think this is hard to do at all, but I'm not the expert.  Anyone else have some insight?  THANKS.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||whamel||09-01-2000||08:44 AM||||So basically what you want is a minute timer with two buttons, start and stop.  I think I used to have some pretty simple schematics for something like that - do a search on the internet.  I just wish I knew what I did with 'em.  I don't think it would be too hard to put together from simple stuff from Radio Shack, but I don't have part numbers for you and there's no RS anywhere near where I am right now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  If I can track anything down I'll let you know, but there are quite a number of people here that are a LOT better at that stuff than I am.  (I can do repair, but design still loses me sometimes.)<BR>But I think the G-Tech is worth noting though.  It will give you a LOT more information that you will probably be after eventually.  ||||reg||1
